---
title: Harness Structured Output
id: structured-outputs-harnesses
order: 6
description: "Ask a coding agent in a sandbox to inspect a repo, then read a typed object from chat({ outputSchema }). Works with Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Grok Build, and acpCompatible."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - structured outputs
  - harness
  - claude code
  - codex
  - opencode
  - grok build
  - outputSchema
  - sandbox
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You asked a coding agent to inspect a repository. The agent streams tool calls and prose. You need a typed object you can store or render, not a wall of text to parse."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" on the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call. The harness runs its native tools. Then you get a validated object from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"await chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" or from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat().final"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page is for sandbox harness adapters:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/claude-code","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude Code"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/codex","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Codex"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/opencode","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenCode"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/grok-build","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok Build"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/acp-compatible","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ACP-Compatible"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you only extract JSON from a prompt and you do not need a sandbox, use "},{"type":"link","href":"./one-shot","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One-Shot Extraction"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with an HTTP adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"define-the-schema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Define the schema"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { z } from \"zod\";\n\nexport const ReportSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string(),\n  oneLiner: z.string(),\n  audience: z.string(),\n  mainPackages: z.array(\n    z.object({\n      name: z.string(),\n      role: z.string(),\n    }),\n  ),\n  howToRun: z.string(),\n});","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=harness-output"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The return type follows from the schema. You do not need a cast."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"server-sandbox-plus-outputschema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server: sandbox plus outputSchema"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The harness needs a sandbox. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox(...)"},{"type":"text","value":". If the client reads the stream, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream: true"},{"type":"text","value":". Without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream: true"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":", not SSE."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\nimport {\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\";\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-report\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: \"TanStack/ai\" }),\n  }),\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const body: unknown = await request.json();\n  const messages =\n    typeof body === \"object\" &&\n    body !== null &&\n    \"messages\" in body &&\n    Array.isArray(body.messages)\n      ? body.messages\n      : [];\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n    messages,\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n    stream: true,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=harness-output"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Swap the adapter to change the agent:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codexText(\"gpt-5.3-codex\")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opencodeText(\"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5\")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokBuildText(\"composer-2.5\")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatibleText(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" for any ACP CLI. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/acp-compatible","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ACP-Compatible"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The typed object arrives as a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":" event. Tool activity streams first."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"client-read-parts-and-final","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client: read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parts"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"final"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The assistant message holds the live run. Walk "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages[].parts"},{"type":"text","value":" for tool calls, reasoning, and the typed object. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat().final"},{"type":"text","value":" is a shortcut for the latest "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output"},{"type":"text","value":" part."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nfunction RepoReport() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, final } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/repo-report\"),\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <button\n        disabled={isLoading}\n        onClick={() => sendMessage(\"What is this repository about?\")}\n      >\n        Run report\n      </button>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) => {\n            if (part.type === \"thinking\") {\n              return <p key={index}>{part.content}</p>;\n            }\n            if (part.type === \"tool-call\") {\n              return (\n                <p key={part.id}>\n                  {part.name} ({part.state})\n                </p>\n              );\n            }\n            if (part.type === \"text\") {\n              return <p key={index}>{part.content}</p>;\n            }\n            if (part.type === \"structured-output\") {\n              const report = part.data ?? part.partial;\n              return report?.name ? <h2 key={index}>{report.name}</h2> : null;\n            }\n            return null;\n          })}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      {final ? <p>{final.oneLiner}</p> : null}\n    </>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=harness-output"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each part type:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"thinking"},{"type":"text","value":": harness reasoning, when the agent emits it"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tool-call"},{"type":"text","value":": native harness tools such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Read"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Bash"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text"},{"type":"text","value":": prose the agent writes before the JSON"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output"},{"type":"text","value":": the schema object. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.data"},{"type":"text","value":" is the validated value. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.partial"},{"type":"text","value":" is a progressive parse when the adapter streams JSON text. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.raw"},{"type":"text","value":" is the source string."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"final"},{"type":"text","value":" is typed as the schema. It stays "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" until "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":" arrives. It always matches the latest assistant turn. Older turns stay on their own "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output"},{"type":"text","value":" parts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partial"},{"type":"text","value":" stays empty on harness adapters. The object is not streamed field by field. Render tool calls from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" while you wait. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./streaming","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming UIs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partial"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"final"},{"type":"text","value":" shape."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"persist-the-typed-object","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persist the typed object"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":" next to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":". The engine stores the completed\nstructured-output part on the transcript. A new message id keeps harness prose\nand the structured object as two assistant messages. The last text message id\nkeeps both on one message. A reload hydrates that transcript through\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconstructChat"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/chat-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat Persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\nimport { withPersistence } from \"@tanstack/ai-persistence\";\nimport {\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\";\nimport { persistence } from \"./persistence\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst ReportSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string(),\n  oneLiner: z.string(),\n});\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-report\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: \"TanStack/ai\" }),\n  }),\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const body: unknown = await request.json();\n  const messages =\n    typeof body === \"object\" &&\n    body !== null &&\n    \"messages\" in body &&\n    Array.isArray(body.messages)\n      ? body.messages\n      : [];\n  const threadId =\n    typeof body === \"object\" &&\n    body !== null &&\n    \"threadId\" in body &&\n    typeof body.threadId === \"string\"\n      ? body.threadId\n      : undefined;\n  const runId =\n    typeof body === \"object\" &&\n    body !== null &&\n    \"runId\" in body &&\n    typeof body.runId === \"string\"\n      ? body.runId\n      : undefined;\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n    messages,\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n    stream: true,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox), withPersistence(persistence)],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=harness-persist"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-each-harness-applies-the-schema","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How each harness applies the schema"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How the schema is applied"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude Code"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Native "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json-schema"},{"type":"text","value":" flag on the same turn. The value is inline JSON, not a file path."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Codex"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Native "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--output-schema"},{"type":"text","value":" flag on the same turn. Assistant text streams as Codex writes it. The last message is also the schema object."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenCode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Schema is added to the prompt. The adapter parses the last assistant text."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok Build"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Schema is added to the prompt. The adapter parses the last assistant text."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ACP compatible"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Schema is added to the prompt. The adapter parses the last assistant text."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenCode, Grok Build, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"acpCompatible"},{"type":"text","value":" parse JSON from the last assistant message. That parse fails if the message is not JSON. If the job is extract-only and you do not need a sandbox, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openai"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-grok"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"approval-gates-and-client-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Approval gates and client tools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness adapters run tools inside the sandbox. They do not pause for a browser round-trip."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A tool without a server "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute()"},{"type":"text","value":" fails fast."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A tool with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"needsApproval"},{"type":"text","value":" fails fast."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you need approval gates or client tools, use "},{"type":"link","href":"./with-tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with an HTTP adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"script-without-a-ui","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Script without a UI"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you do not stream to a browser, omit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream: true"},{"type":"text","value":". The promise resolves with the typed object."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const report = await chat({\n  adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What is this repository about?\" }],\n  outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n});\n\nreport.name;\nreport.oneLiner;","lang":"typescript","meta":"group=harness-output"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"try-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Try it"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The React chat example includes a repo-report page."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-chat","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/ts-react-chat"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/repo-report"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick Claude Code, Grok Build, ACP compatible, or Codex."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick Auth. The default is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API key"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Use "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Host login"}]},{"type":"text","value":" if the machine already ran "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude login"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok login"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codex login"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run the report. The page renders tool calls and reasoning from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages[].parts"},{"type":"text","value":". It reads the typed object from the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output"},{"type":"text","value":" part and from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat().final"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The page clones "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TanStack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":" into a sandbox, asks the agent to inspect it, and shows the validated report."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude Code does not need you to accept a trust dialog for that clone. The adapter loads only user settings, so the clone's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".claude/settings.json"},{"type":"text","value":" does not block headless "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-p"},{"type":"text","value":". Host login uses your host "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude login"},{"type":"text","value":". The sandbox type does not pick this. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Auth"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"define-the-schema","text":"Define the schema","level":2},{"id":"server-sandbox-plus-outputschema","text":"Server: sandbox plus outputSchema","level":2},{"id":"client-read-parts-and-final","text":"Client: read parts and final","level":2},{"id":"persist-the-typed-object","text":"Persist the typed object","level":2},{"id":"how-each-harness-applies-the-schema","text":"How each harness applies the schema","level":2},{"id":"approval-gates-and-client-tools","text":"Approval gates and client tools","level":2},{"id":"script-without-a-ui","text":"Script without a UI","level":2},{"id":"try-it","text":"Try it","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou asked a coding agent to inspect a repository. The agent streams tool calls and prose. You need a typed object you can store or render, not a wall of text to parse.\n\nPass `outputSchema` on the same `chat()` call. The harness runs its native tools. Then you get a validated object from `await chat()` or from `useChat().final`.\n\nThis page is for sandbox harness adapters:\n\n- [Claude Code](../adapters/claude-code)\n- [Codex](../adapters/codex)\n- [OpenCode](../adapters/opencode)\n- [Grok Build](../adapters/grok-build)\n- [ACP-Compatible](../adapters/acp-compatible) (`acpCompatible`)\n\nIf you only extract JSON from a prompt and you do not need a sandbox, use [One-Shot Extraction](./one-shot) with an HTTP adapter.\n\n## Define the schema\n\n```typescript group=harness-output\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nexport const ReportSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string(),\n  oneLiner: z.string(),\n  audience: z.string(),\n  mainPackages: z.array(\n    z.object({\n      name: z.string(),\n      role: z.string(),\n    }),\n  ),\n  howToRun: z.string(),\n});\n```\n\nThe return type follows from the schema. You do not need a cast.\n\n## Server: sandbox plus outputSchema\n\nThe harness needs a sandbox. Pass `withSandbox(...)`. If the client reads the stream, pass `stream: true`. Without `stream: true`, `chat()` returns a `Promise`, not SSE.\n\n```typescript group=harness-output\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\nimport {\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\";\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-report\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: \"TanStack/ai\" }),\n  }),\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const body: unknown = await request.json();\n  const messages =\n    typeof body === \"object\" &&\n    body !== null &&\n    \"messages\" in body &&\n    Array.isArray(body.messages)\n      ? body.messages\n      : [];\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n    messages,\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n    stream: true,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nSwap the adapter to change the agent:\n\n- `codexText(\"gpt-5.3-codex\")`\n- `opencodeText(\"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5\")`\n- `grokBuildText(\"composer-2.5\")`\n- `acpCompatibleText(...)` for any ACP CLI. See [ACP-Compatible](../adapters/acp-compatible).\n\nThe typed object arrives as a `structured-output.complete` event. Tool activity streams first.\n\n## Client: read `parts` and `final`\n\nThe assistant message holds the live run. Walk `messages[].parts` for tool calls, reasoning, and the typed object. `useChat().final` is a shortcut for the latest `structured-output` part.\n\n```tsx group=harness-output\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nfunction RepoReport() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, final } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/repo-report\"),\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <button\n        disabled={isLoading}\n        onClick={() => sendMessage(\"What is this repository about?\")}\n      >\n        Run report\n      </button>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) => {\n            if (part.type === \"thinking\") {\n              return <p key={index}>{part.content}</p>;\n            }\n            if (part.type === \"tool-call\") {\n              return (\n                <p key={part.id}>\n                  {part.name} ({part.state})\n                </p>\n              );\n            }\n            if (part.type === \"text\") {\n              return <p key={index}>{part.content}</p>;\n            }\n            if (part.type === \"structured-output\") {\n              const report = part.data ?? part.partial;\n              return report?.name ? <h2 key={index}>{report.name}</h2> : null;\n            }\n            return null;\n          })}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      {final ? <p>{final.oneLiner}</p> : null}\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nEach part type:\n\n- `thinking`: harness reasoning, when the agent emits it\n- `tool-call`: native harness tools such as `Read` or `Bash`\n- `text`: prose the agent writes before the JSON\n- `structured-output`: the schema object. `part.data` is the validated value. `part.partial` is a progressive parse when the adapter streams JSON text. `part.raw` is the source string.\n\n`final` is typed as the schema. It stays `null` until `structured-output.complete` arrives. It always matches the latest assistant turn. Older turns stay on their own `structured-output` parts.\n\n`partial` stays empty on harness adapters. The object is not streamed field by field. Render tool calls from `messages` while you wait. See [Streaming UIs](./streaming) for the `partial` / `final` shape.\n\n## Persist the typed object\n\nAdd `withPersistence` next to `withSandbox`. The engine stores the completed\nstructured-output part on the transcript. A new message id keeps harness prose\nand the structured object as two assistant messages. The last text message id\nkeeps both on one message. A reload hydrates that transcript through\n`reconstructChat`. See [Chat Persistence](../persistence/chat-persistence).\n\n```typescript group=harness-persist\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\nimport { withPersistence } from \"@tanstack/ai-persistence\";\nimport {\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\";\nimport { persistence } from \"./persistence\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst ReportSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string(),\n  oneLiner: z.string(),\n});\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-report\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: \"TanStack/ai\" }),\n  }),\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const body: unknown = await request.json();\n  const messages =\n    typeof body === \"object\" &&\n    body !== null &&\n    \"messages\" in body &&\n    Array.isArray(body.messages)\n      ? body.messages\n      : [];\n  const threadId =\n    typeof body === \"object\" &&\n    body !== null &&\n    \"threadId\" in body &&\n    typeof body.threadId === \"string\"\n      ? body.threadId\n      : undefined;\n  const runId =\n    typeof body === \"object\" &&\n    body !== null &&\n    \"runId\" in body &&\n    typeof body.runId === \"string\"\n      ? body.runId\n      : undefined;\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n    messages,\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n    stream: true,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox), withPersistence(persistence)],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## How each harness applies the schema\n\n| Adapter | How the schema is applied |\n|---|---|\n| Claude Code | Native `--json-schema` flag on the same turn. The value is inline JSON, not a file path. |\n| Codex | Native `--output-schema` flag on the same turn. Assistant text streams as Codex writes it. The last message is also the schema object. |\n| OpenCode | Schema is added to the prompt. The adapter parses the last assistant text. |\n| Grok Build | Schema is added to the prompt. The adapter parses the last assistant text. |\n| ACP compatible | Schema is added to the prompt. The adapter parses the last assistant text. |\n\nOpenCode, Grok Build, and `acpCompatible` parse JSON from the last assistant message. That parse fails if the message is not JSON. If the job is extract-only and you do not need a sandbox, use `@tanstack/ai-openai` or `@tanstack/ai-grok`.\n\n## Approval gates and client tools\n\nHarness adapters run tools inside the sandbox. They do not pause for a browser round-trip.\n\n- A tool without a server `execute()` fails fast.\n- A tool with `needsApproval` fails fast.\n\nIf you need approval gates or client tools, use [With Tools](./with-tools) with an HTTP adapter.\n\n## Script without a UI\n\nIf you do not stream to a browser, omit `stream: true`. The promise resolves with the typed object.\n\n```typescript group=harness-output\nconst report = await chat({\n  adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What is this repository about?\" }],\n  outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n});\n\nreport.name;\nreport.oneLiner;\n```\n\n## Try it\n\nThe React chat example includes a repo-report page.\n\n1. Open [`examples/ts-react-chat`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-chat).\n2. Open `/repo-report`.\n3. Pick Claude Code, Grok Build, ACP compatible, or Codex.\n4. Pick Auth. The default is **API key**. Use **Host login** if the machine already ran `claude login`, `grok login`, or `codex login`.\n5. Run the report. The page renders tool calls and reasoning from `messages[].parts`. It reads the typed object from the `structured-output` part and from `useChat().final`.\n\nThe page clones `TanStack/ai` into a sandbox, asks the agent to inspect it, and shows the validated report.\n\nClaude Code does not need you to accept a trust dialog for that clone. The adapter loads only user settings, so the clone's `.claude/settings.json` does not block headless `-p`. Host login uses your host `claude login`. The sandbox type does not pick this. See [Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Harness Structured Output\nid: structured-outputs-harnesses\norder: 6\ndescription: \"Ask a coding agent in a sandbox to inspect a repo, then read a typed object from chat({ outputSchema }). Works with Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Grok Build, and acpCompatible.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - structured outputs\n  - harness\n  - claude code\n  - codex\n  - opencode\n  - grok build\n  - outputSchema\n  - sandbox\n---\n\nYou asked a coding agent to inspect a repository. The agent streams tool calls and prose. You need a typed object you can store or render, not a wall of text to parse.\n\nPass `outputSchema` on the same `chat()` call. The harness runs its native tools. Then you get a validated object from `await chat()` or from `useChat().final`.\n\nThis page is for sandbox harness adapters:\n\n- [Claude Code](../adapters/claude-code)\n- [Codex](../adapters/codex)\n- [OpenCode](../adapters/opencode)\n- [Grok Build](../adapters/grok-build)\n- [ACP-Compatible](../adapters/acp-compatible) (`acpCompatible`)\n\nIf you only extract JSON from a prompt and you do not need a sandbox, use [One-Shot Extraction](./one-shot) with an HTTP adapter.\n\n## Define the schema\n\n```typescript group=harness-output\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nexport const ReportSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string(),\n  oneLiner: z.string(),\n  audience: z.string(),\n  mainPackages: z.array(\n    z.object({\n      name: z.string(),\n      role: z.string(),\n    }),\n  ),\n  howToRun: z.string(),\n});\n```\n\nThe return type follows from the schema. You do not need a cast.\n\n## Server: sandbox plus outputSchema\n\nThe harness needs a sandbox. Pass `withSandbox(...)`. If the client reads the stream, pass `stream: true`. Without `stream: true`, `chat()` returns a `Promise`, not SSE.\n\n```typescript group=harness-output\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\nimport {\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\";\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-report\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: \"TanStack/ai\" }),\n  }),\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const body: unknown = await request.json();\n  const messages =\n    typeof body === \"object\" &&\n    body !== null &&\n    \"messages\" in body &&\n    Array.isArray(body.messages)\n      ? body.messages\n      : [];\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n    messages,\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n    stream: true,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nSwap the adapter to change the agent:\n\n- `codexText(\"gpt-5.3-codex\")`\n- `opencodeText(\"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5\")`\n- `grokBuildText(\"composer-2.5\")`\n- `acpCompatibleText(...)` for any ACP CLI. See [ACP-Compatible](../adapters/acp-compatible).\n\nThe typed object arrives as a `structured-output.complete` event. Tool activity streams first.\n\n## Client: read `parts` and `final`\n\nThe assistant message holds the live run. Walk `messages[].parts` for tool calls, reasoning, and the typed object. `useChat().final` is a shortcut for the latest `structured-output` part.\n\n```tsx group=harness-output\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nfunction RepoReport() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, final } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/repo-report\"),\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <button\n        disabled={isLoading}\n        onClick={() => sendMessage(\"What is this repository about?\")}\n      >\n        Run report\n      </button>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) => {\n            if (part.type === \"thinking\") {\n              return <p key={index}>{part.content}</p>;\n            }\n            if (part.type === \"tool-call\") {\n              return (\n                <p key={part.id}>\n                  {part.name} ({part.state})\n                </p>\n              );\n            }\n            if (part.type === \"text\") {\n              return <p key={index}>{part.content}</p>;\n            }\n            if (part.type === \"structured-output\") {\n              const report = part.data ?? part.partial;\n              return report?.name ? <h2 key={index}>{report.name}</h2> : null;\n            }\n            return null;\n          })}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      {final ? <p>{final.oneLiner}</p> : null}\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nEach part type:\n\n- `thinking`: harness reasoning, when the agent emits it\n- `tool-call`: native harness tools such as `Read` or `Bash`\n- `text`: prose the agent writes before the JSON\n- `structured-output`: the schema object. `part.data` is the validated value. `part.partial` is a progressive parse when the adapter streams JSON text. `part.raw` is the source string.\n\n`final` is typed as the schema. It stays `null` until `structured-output.complete` arrives. It always matches the latest assistant turn. Older turns stay on their own `structured-output` parts.\n\n`partial` stays empty on harness adapters. The object is not streamed field by field. Render tool calls from `messages` while you wait. See [Streaming UIs](./streaming) for the `partial` / `final` shape.\n\n## Persist the typed object\n\nAdd `withPersistence` next to `withSandbox`. The engine stores the completed\nstructured-output part on the transcript. A new message id keeps harness prose\nand the structured object as two assistant messages. The last text message id\nkeeps both on one message. A reload hydrates that transcript through\n`reconstructChat`. See [Chat Persistence](../persistence/chat-persistence).\n\n```typescript group=harness-persist\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\nimport { withPersistence } from \"@tanstack/ai-persistence\";\nimport {\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\";\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\";\nimport { persistence } from \"./persistence\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst ReportSchema = z.object({\n  name: z.string(),\n  oneLiner: z.string(),\n});\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-report\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: \"TanStack/ai\" }),\n  }),\n});\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const body: unknown = await request.json();\n  const messages =\n    typeof body === \"object\" &&\n    body !== null &&\n    \"messages\" in body &&\n    Array.isArray(body.messages)\n      ? body.messages\n      : [];\n  const threadId =\n    typeof body === \"object\" &&\n    body !== null &&\n    \"threadId\" in body &&\n    typeof body.threadId === \"string\"\n      ? body.threadId\n      : undefined;\n  const runId =\n    typeof body === \"object\" &&\n    body !== null &&\n    \"runId\" in body &&\n    typeof body.runId === \"string\"\n      ? body.runId\n      : undefined;\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n    messages,\n    outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n    stream: true,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n    middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox), withPersistence(persistence)],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## How each harness applies the schema\n\n| Adapter | How the schema is applied |\n|---|---|\n| Claude Code | Native `--json-schema` flag on the same turn. The value is inline JSON, not a file path. |\n| Codex | Native `--output-schema` flag on the same turn. Assistant text streams as Codex writes it. The last message is also the schema object. |\n| OpenCode | Schema is added to the prompt. The adapter parses the last assistant text. |\n| Grok Build | Schema is added to the prompt. The adapter parses the last assistant text. |\n| ACP compatible | Schema is added to the prompt. The adapter parses the last assistant text. |\n\nOpenCode, Grok Build, and `acpCompatible` parse JSON from the last assistant message. That parse fails if the message is not JSON. If the job is extract-only and you do not need a sandbox, use `@tanstack/ai-openai` or `@tanstack/ai-grok`.\n\n## Approval gates and client tools\n\nHarness adapters run tools inside the sandbox. They do not pause for a browser round-trip.\n\n- A tool without a server `execute()` fails fast.\n- A tool with `needsApproval` fails fast.\n\nIf you need approval gates or client tools, use [With Tools](./with-tools) with an HTTP adapter.\n\n## Script without a UI\n\nIf you do not stream to a browser, omit `stream: true`. The promise resolves with the typed object.\n\n```typescript group=harness-output\nconst report = await chat({\n  adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What is this repository about?\" }],\n  outputSchema: ReportSchema,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n});\n\nreport.name;\nreport.oneLiner;\n```\n\n## Try it\n\nThe React chat example includes a repo-report page.\n\n1. Open [`examples/ts-react-chat`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-chat).\n2. Open `/repo-report`.\n3. Pick Claude Code, Grok Build, ACP compatible, or Codex.\n4. Pick Auth. The default is **API key**. Use **Host login** if the machine already ran `claude login`, `grok login`, or `codex login`.\n5. Run the report. The page renders tool calls and reasoning from `messages[].parts`. It reads the typed object from the `structured-output` part and from `useChat().final`.\n\nThe page clones `TanStack/ai` into a sandbox, asks the agent to inspect it, and shows the validated report.\n\nClaude Code does not need you to accept a trust dialog for that clone. The adapter loads only user settings, so the clone's `.claude/settings.json` does not block headless `-p`. Host login uses your host `claude login`. The sandbox type does not pick this. See [Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth).\n"}
